    <name>
      <text>Partial Variation 4 - Taxi fare graph (interactive)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A taxi in Nairobi charges a fixed booking fee plus a charge for every kilometre travelled: \(C = kd + b\), where \(C\) is the cost in hundreds of Ksh and \(d\) is the distance in km. The graph shows this relationship, and \(P\) is a point on the line.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans3="ans3Ref" width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
var line = board.create('segment', [[0,{#pb#}],[9,{#pb+9*pk#}]], {strokeColor:'blue', fixed:true});
var P = board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pCP#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4});
var A = board.create('point', [1,1], {name:'A', snapToGrid:true, snapSizeX:1, snapSizeY:1, size:5});
stack_jxg.bind_point(ans3Ref, A);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>(a) Read from the graph where the line crosses the vertical axis. This is the fixed booking fee, \(b\).</p>
<p>\(b = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Use the point \(P\) and your value of \(b\) to find the rate \(k\) (the cost for each km).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) Drag the point \(A\) to the point on the line where \(d = {@px3@}\) km. The coordinates of \(A\) appear in the box below.</p>
<p>\(A = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The line crosses the vertical axis at \({@pb@}\), so \(b = {@pb@}\).</p>
<p>The point \(P\) is \(({@pr@}, {@pCP@})\). Substitute into \(C = kd + b\): \({@pCP@} = k({@pr@}) + {@pb@}\), so \(k = \frac{ {@pCP@} - {@pb@} }{ {@pr@} } = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>The line is \(C = {@pk@}d + {@pb@}\). When \(d = {@px3@}\): \(C = {@pk@}({@px3@}) + {@pb@} = {@pk*px3+pb@}\), so \(A = ({@px3@}, {@pk*px3+pb@})\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
